   "subtitle": "Lesson 03 · Foundation",
   "text": "\"Will it hold on launch day?\" is a question with a numerical answer, and the arithmetic takes a minute. A dozen constants, four multiplications and one honest rounding — and the design's hard part introduces itself before a line of it is written. A guess and an estimate look the same and are not Ground floor A dozen constants, and the discipline of rounding The idea Four ways an estimate lies, and one sanity check The danger Estimate any system in a minute See it Five questions Test it Three moments where the arithmetic is the answer Use it Five questions worth asking Take away Every word, in plain English Reference",
