   "title": "Five questions worth asking",
   "subtitle": "Lesson 04 · Take away",
   "text": "\"If the next request lands on a different server, does this still work?\" The one question that finds hidden state. Ask it of the session, the uploaded file, the counter, the cached value — everything the code keeps between requests. Whatever answers no is the bug the second server will expose. \"Where does the session live — memory, a store, or the token?\" Three answers with three different failure modes. Memory cannot survive a second server; a store is a box that must not die; a token cannot be revoked before it expires. There is no free option, only the one whose cost you can live with. \"Are we sticky? When do we take it off?\" Sticky sessions are a bridge, not a destination. If the answer to the second half is \"we hadn't thought about it\", the crutch has quietly become the design, and a deploy still logs everyone out. \"What does our health check actually test?\" If it only proves the process is up, it will keep a broken server taking traffic. If it fails on every shared-dependency blip, one blip takes the whole fleet down. It should test what this server needs to do its own job — no less, no more. \"Can we lose a server right now without anyone noticing?\" The definition of stateless, phrased as a dare. If the honest answer is yes, autoscaling, rolling deploys and surviving a crash all come for free. If it is no, find the note that only one server is keeping. Tiếng Việt Bạn không cần thuộc kỹ thuật nào. Chỉ cần một câu hỏi cho mọi state giữa các request — \"request sau rơi sang server khác có còn chạy không?\" — biết session đang ở đâu và cái giá của nơi đó, và trả lời được câu: mất một server ngay bây giờ có ai nhận ra không.",
