   "why": "For money, two truths is worse than a pause: charging or not-charging must never disagree across copies. That is CP — refuse writes that cannot be confirmed, so nothing is ever wrong, and accept that some users cannot pay during the split. The cost is real (errors, briefly) and it is the right cost. AP here would mean accepting charges on both sides and reconciling later, which for money means double charges or a seat sold twice. The database does have a default, and accepting it blindly is exactly how this goes wrong."
